-- title:
--   A single moduli place above a supersingular place, H₁ level
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an integer $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$.
--
--   **Reduction data over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.** Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places (in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.Place`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22): a valuation subring of the top field containing the image of the base field, distinct from the whole field, whose valuation subring is a principal ideal ring) of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` $=\kappa_A(j,j_{M'})$ over $\kappa_A=$ `ResidueField A`, and assume (`hW`) that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the places satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`. Assume (`hle`) that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, is contained in `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: it provides a valuation subring `R₀.integers` whose intersection with the base field is $A$, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the reduction field with kernel the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, compatible with the residue map of $A$, a degree-preserving map `R₀.placeMap` on places compatible with orders of vanishing, and a scaling property producing nonzero residues. Assume (`hR₀`) that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally let $s\in W$ be one of these supersingular places.
--
--   **The arithmetic base field.** Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$, and write $\mathcal O =$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ` require: $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring; its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; it is a Henselian local ring; its residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField ↥𝒪` is algebraically closed; and every element of $A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity and the level subgroup.** Let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and assume (`hιξ`) that some ring homomorphism $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ with (`hH₁`) $H_1 =$ `levelH q M'` $\sqcap$ the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; here `levelH q M'` is the kernel of `ZMod.unitsMap` for $q\mid q^2M'$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, so $H_1$ is the group of units of $\mathbb Z/q^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0$ in `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` given (`hK`) by `laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, the $k_0$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the level-$H_1$ function field of level $q^2M'$; $K$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, compatibly with $\mathcal O\to k_0\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb ↥k₀ jq` (`hj`), assumed nonzero.
--
--   **Transport hypotheses for the Weierstrass level data.** The hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL` assert stability under variable change over arbitrary $\mathcal O$-algebras $T$: `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` (the defining equations for $(x_P,y_P)$ together with $(\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g})(x_P)=0$ and $x_Q=x_P$, $y_Q=y_P$) passes to $C\bullet W$ with $D$ replaced by `D.variableChange C`; `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` passes to $C\bullet W$ with $h$ replaced by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; and any divisor $h$ of `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` transports to a divisor `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` of `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓg n (u^{-2}(x-r))`. Let $\mathcal G$ be a family `GroupLaws ↥𝒪` of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`: the group law is computed by a points evaluation) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: the identity section is cut out by an origin chart homomorphism killing $x/y$ and $z/y$), and let $\mathcal T$ be a `LevelTransport ↥𝒪 𝒢 q` assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`: the transported $P$- and $Q$-sections agree with the originals after the relevant graded-ring comparison maps). The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every projective Weierstrass model over an $\mathcal O$-algebra, graded ring homomorphisms realising a given variable change, respectively a given $\mathcal O$-algebra map on coefficients, satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom` respectively `IsCoefficientHom` and dominating the irrelevant ideal.
--
--   **The moduli package and the point over $K$.** Write $\mathcal R =$ `rigidDataH1Pow ↥𝒪 ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`, the rigid Weierstrass datum obtained by restricting the product of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-power component, the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-component and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component along the link condition `IsGamma1Link`. Let $P_0$ be a `LevelModuliPackageAbs ↥𝒪` for `𝒭.toLevelModuliDatum`: an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point `P₀.univ` through which every point over every $\mathcal O$-algebra factors uniquely. Let $x_0$ be a point of the datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant is (`hx₀`) the Laurent series `jqNModC ↥k₀ q`. Let $\mathrm{clC}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from $B_0$ to the chart algebra $\mathcal A =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ↥𝒪 ↥K j` (the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra `chartAlg ↥𝒪 ↥K {j}` of $K$, the finite chart of the two-chart integral model attached to $j$), agreeing (`hclC`) with `P₀.classify x₀` after the inclusion $\mathcal A\subseteq K$.
--
--   **The Tate-point pin `hμ`.** There exist a variable change $C$ over `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` and a raw datum $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ with $[r]=x_0$, such that, writing $(x_T,y_T) =$ `tateToricPoint ↥k₀ q (ξ^q)` for the toric point at the unit $\xi^q$ (a primitive $\ell_g$-th root of unity): (i) $C.u\,(2x_T + \tfrac16) = 2y_T + x_T$, $C.r = -\tfrac1{12}$, $C.s = -\tfrac12$, $C.t = \tfrac1{24}$ as constant Laurent series; (ii) the curve of $r$, base changed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals $C\bullet$ `tateBase ↥k₀ q`; (iii) for every prime $p\mid M'$, every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f:k_0\to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta\in F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` and then coefficientwise by $f$, equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of $C$ (mapped by $f$) in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (v_p(M'))` applied to $\prod_{1\le a\le p^{v_p(M')}/2,\ p\nmid a}\bigl(X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,q\,(\zeta^a))_1\bigr)$; (iv) the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-component $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$, pushed to `LaurentSeries ↥k₀`, equals the variable change by $C$ of the `LevelPData` with $x_P=x_Q=x_T$ and $y_P=y_Q=y_T$; and (v) there exist $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose Laurent series are the four coordinates of the variable change by $C$ of `cuspData ↥k₀ q (ξ^{ℓg}) ![1,0] ![0,-1]` (the unit $\xi^{\ell_g}$ being a primitive $q$-th root of unity), and such that the Drinfeld sections $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P$ and $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.Q$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there is a single place $v$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ M'` over $\kappa =$ `ResidueField ↥𝒪` with the following property. For every maximal ideal $y$ of the chart algebra $\mathcal A$ and every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\psi:\mathcal A\to\kappa$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (i.e. $\psi c = 0 \iff c\in y$), assume the following hovering condition: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, such that (a) at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the order of $j_q$ is $\ge 0$ the order of $g$ is also $\ge 0$, and (b) the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and such that `coeffEmb ↥k₀ g` lies in $K$ and the resulting element of $K$ lies in $\mathcal A$: for every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the element of $\mathcal A$ determined by `coeffEmb ↥k₀ g` minus the image of $c$ under $\mathcal O\to\mathcal A$ lies in $y$.
--
--   Then for every raw datum $x$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\kappa$ whose class $[x]$ in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ is the image of the universal point `P₀.univ` under the map induced by $\psi\circ\mathrm{clC}$, and for every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x$ such that $g$ has additive order $M'$ and, for every prime $p\mid M'$, every $n$ and every nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ of the curve with $n\cdot g=(x_1,y_1)$ and $n\cdot g$ of additive order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the coordinate $x_1$ is a root of $x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$: the $\Gamma_0(M')$-moduli point in `ModuliPoint M' κ` represented by the pair consisting of the curve of $x$ (elliptic because its discriminant is a unit) together with the generator $g$ of order $M'$ satisfies `IsModuliPlaceOf κ M'` for $v$, that is, there are a field $\Omega$ over $\kappa$ and a `ModuliTestDatum κ M'` for that moduli point over $\Omega$ whose place, pulled back along the datum's embedding, has valuation subring equal to that of $v$.
--
--   This is the $H_1$-level ($\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$) form of the statement that all $\kappa$-points of the integral $H_1$-chart hovering over one fixed supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ modular function field in characteristic $q$ have their $\Gamma_0(M')$-moduli points supported at one and the same geometric place $v$ of the level-$M'$ function field over the algebraically closed residue field; the Tate-curve pin `hμ` identifies the point over $K$ with the toric (cusp) datum. It is used in the analysis of the specialisation of the $q$-adic degeneration of the modular curve at supersingular points, and feeds the statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.forall_nsmul_eq_zero_and_exists_variableChange_and_inLine_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.forall_nsmul_eq_zero_and_exists_variableChange_and_inLine_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1).
